  <published>2025-12-21T06:43:46+00:00</published>
  <updated>2026-04-15T00:26:46+00:00</updated>
  <media:group>
   <media:title>Winter In The Most Beautiful Mountain Range On Earth. The Ultimate Day Ski Touring</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/SdofEDukjy4?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/SdofEDukjy4/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>We first came to the Dolomites 2021, during Covid-19. It was summer time and we were hiking as much as we could, we saw it at its absolute peak beauty, with lush green mountain pastures leading to giant mountains touring above. We decided to explore this area as much as we could in the winter of 2024/2025. Sextner Stein was one of the most obvious ski tours to do first up. It was a long tour being 10km there and back and over 1100m vertical gain. I wasn't prepared for this at all, my fitness wasn't where I thought it was. But it was well worth it for this amazing view. It wasn't so fun getting back at 7 at night after falling multiple times and getting a tiny bit lost.</media:description>
